## Field Descriptions

### Original Fields

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `indicator_code` | string | Unique identifier (base variable name) |
| `question_type` | enum | `Single`, `MultiSelect`, `Frequency`, `Rating`, `Matrix`, `Ranking`, `Numeric` |
| `indicator_label` | string | Question text |
| `source_variables` | object | Map of SPSS variable code → variable label |
| `transformation_needed` | boolean | Whether transformation is required |
| `transformation_type` | enum or null | `grouping`, `recoding`, `range`, or `null` |
| `transformation_rules` | array or null | Transformation rule items |

### source_variables Field Examples by Question Type

| Question Type | source_variables Example | Description |
|---------------|---------------------------|-------------|
| `Single` | `{"Q1": "Gender"}` | One SPSS variable with category values |
| `MultiSelect` | `{"Q5_1": "TV", "Q5_2": "Radio", ...}` | Multiple sub-variables (checkboxes) |
| `Matrix` | `{"Q10_1_1": "Brand A - Quality", ...}` | Double suffix variables |
| `Ranking` | `{"Q20_RANK1": "First", "Q20_RANK2": "Second"}` | Rank position variables |
| `Numeric` | `{"S1": "Age"}` | One numeric variable |
| `Rating` | `{"Q5": "Satisfaction"}` | One rating variable |
| `Frequency` | `{"Q8": "How often"}` | One frequency variable |

### Transformation Rules (4 Fields)

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `source_values` | array or object | Source values: `["1", "2"]` or `{"min": 18, "max": 25}` |
| `target_value` | string | Target value code |
| `target_label` | string | Target value label |
| `hide_categories` | boolean | Hide component categories in output |

### New CTABLES Fields - Categories

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `explicit` | array or null | Specific values to include: `["1", "2", "3"]` |
| `order` | string | `A` (ascending) or `D` (descending) |
| `sort_key` | string | `VALUE`, `LABEL`, or `COUNT` |
| `include_missing` | boolean | Include user-missing values |
| `totals.show` | boolean | Show total row/column |
| `totals.label` | string | Custom label for total |
| `totals.position` | string | `AFTER` or `BEFORE` |
| `empty` | string | `INCLUDE` or `EXCLUDE` empty categories |

### New CTABLES Fields - Percentages

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `show_row_pct` | boolean | Show row percentage |
| `show_col_pct` | boolean | Show column percentage |
| `show_table_pct` | boolean | Show table percentage |

### New CTABLES Fields - Display

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `variable_label` | string | `DEFAULT`, `NAME`, `LABEL`, `BOTH`, or `NONE` |
| `category_label_position` | string | `AUTO`, `OPPOSITE`, or `LAYER` |
| `hide_empty_categories` | boolean | Hide categories with zero counts |

### New CTABLES Fields - Statistics

| Field | Type | Description |
|-------|------|-------------|
| `count` | boolean | Count of cases |
| `mean` | boolean | Arithmetic mean (scale only) |
| `median` | boolean | Median value (scale only) |
| `mode` | boolean | Most frequent value |
| `stddev` | boolean | Standard deviation (scale only) |
| `variance` | boolean | Variance (scale only) |
| `min` | boolean | Minimum value (scale only) |
| `max` | boolean | Maximum value (scale only) |
| `sum` | boolean | Sum of values (scale only) |
| `range` | boolean | Range = max - min (scale only) |
| `semean` | boolean | Standard error of mean (scale only) |
| `missing` | boolean | Count of missing values |
| `ptile` | number or null | Percentile (0-100) |

## Question Types

| Value | Description | source_variables Example |
|-------|-------------|----------------------------|
| `Single` | Standalone categorical (one response) | `{"Q1": "Gender question"}` |
| `MultiSelect` | Checkboxes (multiple responses possible) | `{"Q5_1": "Option 1", "Q5_2": "Option 2", ...}` |
| `Frequency` | "How often?" (daily/weekly) | `{"Q8": "Frequency question"}` |
| `Rating` | 3-7 point identical scale | `{"Q5": "Satisfaction rating"}` |
| `Matrix` | Grid with double suffix (`_1_1`, `_1_2`) | `{"Q10_1_1": "Brand A - Quality", ...}` |
| `Ranking` | Rank order (rank/first) | `{"Q20_RANK1": "First choice", ...}` |
| `Numeric` | Continuous data | `{"S1": "Age question"}` |

## Transformation Types

| Value | `source_values` Format |
|-------|----------------------|
| `grouping` | `["1.0", "2.0", "3.0"]` |
| `recoding` | `["1.0", "2.0"]` |
| `range` | `{"min": 25, "max": 35}` |

## PSPP Syntax Generation Options

When generating PSPP CTABLES syntax, two approaches are available:

### Option 1: Generate New Variables (DO IF / RECODE)
Creates derived variables using transformation rules:

```spss
DO IF (S1 >= 18 AND S1 <= 25).
  COMPUTE S1_AGE_GROUP = 1.
ELSE IF (S1 >= 26 AND S1 <= 35).
  COMPUTE S1_AGE_GROUP = 2.
...
END IF.
VARIABLE LABELS S1_AGE_GROUP "1 18-25岁 2 26-35岁 ...".
```

### Option 2: Use Original Variables with Subtotals
Uses CTABLES subtotals directly:

```spss
CTABLES
  /TABLE=S1 BY Q1
  /CATEGORIES VARIABLES=S1 [18 THRU 25, 26 THRU 35, ...]
  /CATEGORIES VARIABLES=S1 [1 THRU 3 SUBTOTAL='青年组' HIDECATEGORIES, 4 THRU 6 SUBTOTAL='中老年组' HIDECATEGORIES].
```

The `hide_categories` field in transformation_rules controls whether component categories are hidden when using subtotals.
